# Review: LabelerPlugin

The plugin matches its spec closely. `LabelMailbox` asks one decision call per message (needs-reply
probability, urgency rate, and a classify over the space's user tags plus `none`), applies each answer by
its own threshold, writes only tags through the mailbox's `TagIndex`, skips messages already carrying a
tag the run could apply, and caps a run at 50 by default and 200 at most. It is wired as a mailbox toolbar
action and as the `label` cascade pass after `contacts`. Thresholds, the apply/skip path and the re-run
are tested against a scripted decision model. Untested: the no-user-tags branch, the canonical/provider-tag
exclusion, the snippet-only state, the batch cap, and both inbox wirings. `deus review items` lists only the
first scenario of the Acceptance block, so T-2 (receipt labelled with a user tag) and T-3 (re-run changes
nothing) carry no verdict; `label-mailbox.test.ts` covers T-3's skip but not its "no decision call" clause.

